{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789259401,"nonce":"ySPNwpcl68XG4KbD0QwgSwZ4dRU=","message":"Landed as 8d3b0f4e107b266d337936fd4ea447cf82736209. Per-cycle cost of a hosted binary_trees cycle under tiered\nWLIFT_GC_STRESS=1, release, medians over alternating runs on a quiet\nmachine: wlift 0.628 ms, hosted before 1.796 ms, hosted after 0.628 ms.\ndelta_blue stress: wlift 0.028, before 0.054, after 0.025. Interpreter\nstress (35,857 cycles, deterministic counters identical before/after):\n195.6 s -\u003e 63.6-71.3 s against wlift's 53-57 s.\n\nWhat moved the numbers, by phase of a hosted cycle:\n- wren_lift's mark through the adapter's claim (was 1.08 ms of ~1.8):\n  the claim became a bit in the object's prefix word instead of a\n  side-table resolve under the lock; plain loads/stores since the caller\n  holds the lock and no marker runs; the cross-crate claim inlined.\n- pin pass (0.24): one side-table read per pin, then, with the prefix\n  bit, no resolve at all: claim_start is idempotent and address-ordered.\n- core mark (0.17, nearly all the anchor re-checking every pin): the\n  anchor stands down during collect_end's own collection, where every\n  surviving pin is already claimed.\n- core sweep (0.35, ~90% the drop pass walking every traced block):\n  Block.has_traced became has_drop, set only when the descriptor at word\n  zero has a drop hook; the adapter's objects never do.\nshould_collect polling was not measurable.\n\nWhat remains, and where: plain (non-stress) binary_trees wall time is\nstill ~1.5 s hosted vs 0.83 s wlift, and it is the allocation path, not\nthe cycle: per allocation an uncontended lock acquire/release, a\nreentrant re-acquire inside alloc_gen, a side-table lookup for the\nreserved size, a Vec push and an atomic add, about 90 ns over wren_lift's\nbump. Cheap trims if wanted: a locked alloc_gen method on ImmixAllocator\n(saves the reentrant pair), plain store for bytes_since_cycle. The\ninterpreter-stress residue (1.25x) is the pin pass over ~112k pins plus\nthe per-block sweep. Fixed cost unchanged: 16 B prefix + 8 B pin per\nobject.\n\nVerified: caribou 51 tests, caribou-wren 7 (x3), clippy unchanged;\ncorpus 30/30 vs --no-install on the same wren_lift tree, 29/30 vs\nbaseline wlift where test_nested_jit tiered flakes on wlift itself;\nash parity through caribou-ash 120/120. Closing; the allocation-path\ntrims can be a new perf issue when someone wants them.","files":null}]}